WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.050
Lift a book from a desk,
raise it above your head,

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:05.540
and slide it onto a high shelf.

3
00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:09.230
On the shelf, there is more
potential energy than before.

4
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:11.390
Energy is never destroyed.

5
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:12.880
So where is it?

6
00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:13.850
In the book?

7
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:14.960
In the shelf?

8
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:16.830
Somewhere else entirely?

9
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:21.770
In this mission, you'll see how a passenger
on a moving bus has zero kinetic energy,

10
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.510
and 3000 joules, at the same time.

11
00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:30.020
Then you'll draw energy bar charts, tracking
every joule from the start of a motion

12
00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:31.370
to the finish.

13
00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:36.360
Your mission: find out exactly where the
book's new potential energy is stored.
